        "Abstract": "Text-to-image generation models have gained popularity among users worldwide. However, many of these models exhibit a strong bias toward English-speaking cultures, often ignoring or misrepresenting unique cultural characteristics of other language groups, countries, and nationalities. This paper introduces the RusCode benchmark dataset to evaluate the quality of text-to-image generation models containing elements of Russian culture. The dataset consists of 1250 text prompts in Russian and their translations into English, covering various aspects of Russian visual culture."
